Q: 2 dimensional array to string code java A: <p>@dawood-ibn-kareem explain good the possible cause of the failure of the test.</p>

<p>With Java 8 Stream, it's pretty easy to do what you want!</p>

<p>With the input: [[1,2,3], [3,4,5], [5,6,7]]</p>

<pre><code>public static String arrayToString(int[][] a) {
    return Arrays.stream(a)
            .map(s -&gt; Arrays.stream(s)
                            .mapToObj(String::valueOf)
                            .collect(Collectors.joining(" "))
            )
            .collect(Collectors.joining("\n"));
}
</code></pre>

<p>Output:</p>

<pre><code>1 2 3
3 4 5
5 6 7
</code></pre>

<p>Other method, to separate each line of the 2D array without carriage return</p>

<pre><code>public static String arrayToString(int[][] a) {
    return Arrays.stream(a)
            .flatMapToInt(Arrays::stream)
            .mapToObj(String::valueOf)
            .collect(Collectors.joining(" "));
}
</code></pre>

<p>Output</p>

<pre><code>1 2 3 3 4 5 5 6 7
</code></pre>

<p>Have fun!</p>
